# Agent Infrastructure Validation

Before committing changes to rules, skills, hooks, agents, commands, runtime
adapters, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or the agent-system overview, run
`reviewing-agent-infrastructure`. An independent verifier writes
`agent-infrastructure.stamp.md` from the complete working tree; pre-commit
later requires the staged infrastructure manifest to equal that evidence.

Product references such as `architecture-documentation.md`,
`ui-test-conventions.md`, capabilities, and user flows are documentation—not
executable agent infrastructure—and do not trigger a verifier.

Runtime state and descriptive plans are excluded.
